{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a custom Online Store 2.0 section in Liquid called "feature-icons-row".
    
    The section should display three feature items similar to an icon + text row. Use blocks, so I can add up to 3 items.
    
    Each block must contain:
    
    an icon image (image_picker)
    
    a heading (text)
    
    a subtext (richtext or textarea)
    
    a link (URL/page selector)
    
    The icon image must be clickable and behave as a button: clicking anywhere on the icon or the block should go to the block’s link.
    
    Layout:
    
    On desktop, show the blocks horizontally in one row (3 columns).
    
    On mobile, stack them vertically (one per row).
    
    Use a clean, minimal style based on this structure:
    
    icon on the left / top
    
    heading in bold
    
    subtext below
    
    Add section settings:
    
    background color (color picker)
    
    padding top + padding bottom (range)
    
    max width for the content (range, e.g. 800–1400px) and center it.
    
    Add block settings:
    
    icon width (range, e.g. 40–120px)
    
    heading text
    
    subtext text
    
    link (url)
    
    Use semantic HTML, flexbox for layout, and a simple default for font sizes., Continue improving the "feature-icons-row" section you just created.
    
    Responsive behaviour
    
    Use CSS media queries so that:
    
    For screens ≥ 900px, the blocks are arranged in a horizontal row with equal width (3 columns).
    
    For screens < 900px, the blocks stack vertically and span full width.
    
    Also add a section setting called force_vertical_on_desktop (checkbox). If true, always stack blocks vertically even on large screens.
    
    Interactive icons / buttons
    
    Make each block behave like a button:
    
    cursor changes to pointer on hover
    
    add a hover effect: slight scale-up and subtle shadow (e.g. transform: scale(1.03); box-shadow).
    
    add a smooth transition (e.g. 150–200ms) for transform and shadow.
    
    Ensure the whole block is clickable, not only the text.
    
    Extra customization settings
    
    Section settings:
    
    gap between blocks (range, e.g. 8–48px)
    
    text alignment (dropdown: left, center)
    
    Block settings:
    
    icon alignment (dropdown: left, center, top)
    
